<2.5.0>
## Property Areas and Purchase Experience
- Added PolyZone property boundaries as an alternative to radius-based property areas: https://github.com/mkafrin/PolyZone/
- Added admin and realtor tools to capture, edit, export, save, and preview property PolyZones.
- Added property-area previews for players before purchasing or renting a configured house.
- Added property-area previews and configured-house teleport options to the admin menu.

## Property Ownership and Payments
- Added metadata-backed property deed items for purchased and rented properties.
- Added property deed reissuing through configured real-estate agents.
- Added automatic deed replacement when a property is transferred to another player.
- Added cash, gold, and Rol Token support for purchases, rentals, and ledger payments.
- Added per-house rental controls and an option for tenants to end rentals early.

## Taxes and Rent
- New purchases, rentals, and admin-created houses now save their actual purchase date.
- Taxes and rent are collected monthly on each property's purchase-date anniversary.
- Existing properties without a purchase date receive a legacy fallback based on `Config.TaxDay`.
- Added `last_tax_processed_at` tracking to prevent duplicate monthly charges.
- Added overdue-property restrictions and an admin workflow to release properties for ledger payment.

## Administration, Security, and Reliability
- Expanded admin property details, overdue filtering, boundary previews, and inventory access.
- Added server-side ownership and permission validation for house, door, ledger, furniture, hotel, and admin operations.
- Added protection against simultaneous purchases of the same configured house.
- Improved property boundary detection and reduced enter/leave notification flicker.
- Improved furniture selling and placement validation.
- Replaced the housing-local debug shim with the `BccUtils.Debug` API.

## Furniture Vendors and Localization
- Added support for both `npc.active` and legacy `npc.show` furniture-vendor settings.
- Improved furniture-vendor client performance with adaptive interaction checks.
- Restored the real-estate agent's two-second hold interaction using `BccUtils.Prompts`.
- Localized property-document menu labels and status text.
- Restored and updated the Polish locale for all current housing features.
- Expanded README documentation for the new features and configuration.

